 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? You' a great model for openness. Just being there for her, showing her you value her and her schooling, is the biggest tool. It is. Lots of kids struggle with languages at home, so the act of going along is often enough. Then little lessons after school are a great idea. Ask her what she'd like to practice, and keep it fun. Some kids do. Lots of them. The key is making it normal. If you ask her how her day was, and ask how French is, she'll tell you. Set it as a goal, and agree together what you' do when she achieves it. Then support her without pushing. Remember, practice makes pro.",
